ed time window post-approval.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Ship Item Back\",\"description\":\"The 'Ship Item Back' activity represents the customer shipping the returned item back to the warehouse using a chosen shipping method.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Approve Return\",\"description\":\"The 'Approve Return' activity represents the system's approval of a return request, updating the Return Status to 'Approved'.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"1,14,d\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If a 'Ship Item Back' activity occurs, then a 'Receive Item' activity must eventually occur after it at some point in the same process instance. If 'Ship Item Back' does not occur, the constraint imposes no obligation on the occurrence of 'Receive Item'.\",\"template\":\"Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Ship Item Back\",\"description\":\"The 'Ship Item Back' activity represents the customer shipping the returned item back to the warehouse using a chosen shipping method.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Receive Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Receive Item' activity represents the warehouse receiving the returned item from the customer, updating the Return Status to 'Received'.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Item' activity is permitted to occur only if a 'Receive Item' activity has occurred before it within the same process instance. The 'Inspect Item' must occur within 48 hours of the 'Receive Item' activity, ensuring timely inspection of received items.\",\"template\":\"Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Item' activity represents the warehouse evaluating the condition and quality of the received returned item, assigning an Item Condition score and an Inspection Result.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Receive Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Receive Item' activity represents the warehouse receiving the returned item from the customer, updating the Return Status to 'Received'.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,48,h\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Determine Refund' activity must be followed by a 'Process Refund' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Process Refund' event can occur only if a 'Determine Refund' event has occurred before it. The 'Process Refund' must occur within 0 to 2 days after the 'Determine Refund' activity.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Determine Refund\",\"description\":\"The 'Determine Refund' activity represents the calculation of the refund amount based on the inspection results and return details.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Process Refund\",\"description\":\"The 'Process Refund' activity represents the system executing the refund payment to the customer, updating the Return Status to 'Refunded'.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":\"0,2,d\",\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Restock Item' activity can occur only if it was immediately preceded by an 'Inspect Item' activity where the Inspection Result is 'Acceptable', and no other 'Inspect Item' event is allowed between that 'Inspect Item' and the 'Restock Item'. This ensures a one-to-one and ordered pairing between acceptable inspections and restocking, preventing any 'Restock Item' from occurring without the necessary prior acceptable inspection.\",\"template\":\"Alternate Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Restock Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Restock Item' activity represents the system restocking an acceptable returned item back into inventory, recording the Restock Quantity and updating the Return Status to 'Restocked'.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Item' activity represents the warehouse evaluating the condition and quality of the received returned item, assigning an Item Condition score and an Inspection Result.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Inspection Result is Acceptable\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Dispose Item' activity can occur only if it was immediately preceded by an 'Inspect Item' activity where the Inspection Result is 'Damaged' or 'Unacceptable', and no other 'Inspect Item' event is allowed between that 'Inspect Item' and the 'Dispose Item'. This ensures a one-to-one and ordered pairing between damaged/unacceptable inspections and disposal, preventing any 'Dispose Item' from occurring without the necessary prior inspection with a Damaged or Unacceptable result.\",\"template\":\"Alternate Precedence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Dispose Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Dispose Item' activity represents the system disposing of a damaged or unacceptable returned item, updating the Return Status to 'Disposed'.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Inspect Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Inspect Item' activity represents the warehouse evaluating the condition and quality of the received returned item, assigning an Item Condition score and an Inspection Result.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Inspection Result in (Damaged, Unacceptable)\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"Exactly one of the activities 'Restock Item' or 'Dispose Item' must occur in the process instance, and only if an 'Inspect Item' activity has occurred. The process is compliant if only 'Restock Item' occurs without any occurrence of 'Dispose Item', or only 'Dispose Item' occurs without any occurrence of 'Restock Item'. The process is non-compliant if both 'Restock Item' and 'Dispose Item' occur, or if neither occurs (after inspection). The constraint enforces mutual exclusivity and a mandatory occurrence of one of the two disposition activities, activated conditionally upon the inspection being completed.\",\"template\":\"Exclusive Choice\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Restock Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Restock Item' activity represents the system restocking an acceptable returned item back into inventory, recording the Restock Quantity and updating the Return Status to 'Restocked'.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Dispose Item\",\"description\":\"The 'Dispose Item' activity represents the system disposing of a damaged or unacceptable returned item, updating the Return Status to 'Disposed'.\"},\"activation_condition\":\"A.Return Status is Inspected\",\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null}]}"